            <ArticleTitle>Rhinoconjunctivitis and occupational asthma caused by Diplotaxis erucoides (wall rocket).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Wall rocket (Diplotaxis erucoides) is a common Crucifera plant that grows in European and American vineyards and olive groves. We present the cases of 2 farmers with rhinoconjunctivitis and asthma related to wine-growing tasks during D erucoides pollination (March-April). The aim of this work was to demonstrate that occupational symptoms were caused by D erucoides pollen sensitization. Cutaneous tests, specific IgE measurements, conjunctival and bronchial provocation tests, and peak-flow measurements during working days were performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
